          "§ What turbulence is",
          "Turbulence is irregular, rapid air motion (eddies) superimposed on the general flow, causing bumps, changes of attitude and altitude, and airspeed fluctuations. It is classified by cause into four kinds.",
          "§ 1. Thermal (convective) turbulence",
          "Caused by thermals (rising currents) over unevenly heated ground on sunny days, from the surface up to the cumulus tops, and inside convective cloud. It is worst in the early afternoon over land, in summer, and over dark or dry ground. It is severe to extreme in CB. Cumulus clouds mark the thermals; the air above the cumulus tops (or above the inversion) is usually smooth.",
