          "The vortices are strongest when the aircraft is HEAVY, CLEAN (flaps up) and SLOW, i.e. at a high angle of attack, as during take-off, the initial climb, the final approach and landing. Strength depends mainly on weight and wingspan, and inversely on speed.",
